PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key facts unchanged: chol obligatory ecdysone precursor (cholestanol cannot substitute); 250 mg/L chol supports full cycle; 2 mg/L or 0 mg/L insufficient; 250 mg/L cholestanol yields zero adult survival; maternal egg sterol scales with mother’s diet; cholestanol can supply bulk/sparing role. 

Round-1 split mirrors round-0: majority C/H (Colleagues 2,4,5,7,8,10-14) argue maternal reserve exhausted before/around pupation so Q1 produces death or no eclosion and Q2 (absent reserve + sub-threshold 2 mg/L) produces early larval arrest; minority F/D (Colleagues 1,3,6,9,15) claim reserve suffices for eclosion (then adults die) and sparing rescues 2 mg/L + cholestanol for normal development in Q2. 

Core unresolved tension: interpretation of “zero adult survival” on pure cholestanol (fail to eclose vs. eclose-then-die) and whether sparing effect is strong enough to make 2 mg/L functional without any maternal carry-over. No new empirical thresholds supplied; disagreement persists on reserve exhaustion timing and sparing rescue. Preserve C/H vs. F/D split and sparing assumption for later rounds.}

